<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπειραῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Apeiraean,</i> and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπείρηθεν</span></b> , Adv.
			<i>from Apeire,</i> both in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γρῆϋς Ἀπειραίη . ., τήν ποτ᾽
				Ἀπείρηθεν νέες ἤγαγον.</span>
			<u>Apeire</u> seems to be <i>Limitless-land</i> (from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπειρος</span> B), an imaginary
			place; <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> expl. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπειρωτική.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
